<title>JAPAN: Japan wants U.S. to be flexible on insurance--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan wants U.S. to be flexible on insurance--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vice Finance Minister Tadashi Ogawa said on Monday that Japan wants the United States to be more flexible in negotiations on their bilateral insurance dispute.  </p>
<p>Japan and the United States have been in negotiations since last week in an effort to resolve their insurance dispute before a self-imposed December 15 deadline.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka and acting U.S. Trade Representative (USTR) Charlene Barshefsky are scheduled to meet on Saturday to discuss the issue.</p>
<p>&quot;Japanese and U.S. negotiators are determined to reach an agreement by the deadline. We want to see further flexibility on the part of the U.S.,&quot; Ogawa said.</p>
<p>The two countries have been at odds over deregulation of Japan's domestic insurance market.</p>
</text>
